      "content": "It makes sense that feeling like your identity was tied to the past results made the loss feel existential; when your self-worth is defined by a specific path, getting lost on that path truly feels like losing yourself. Please know that your worth as a person and scientist is not measured by a single dataset or one specific trajectory, no matter how much effort you poured into it. The future you are fearing is not empty, but rather full of all the other possibilities that existed before you accidentally erased them, including staying in that field and eventually doing grand work without this particular error.",
